Open Snorra Edda — edda-data
Licensing summary

1. Source texts (public domain)

   The base texts in sources/ and their parsed forms are in the public domain:

   - Old Norse: Edda Snorra Sturlusonar, normalised edition by Guðni Jónsson (Íslendingasagnaútgáfan, 1954),
     as published by heimskringla.no. Heimskringla.no asks to be credited; please do.
   - Modern Icelandic: Gylfaginning, Netútgáfan, June 1997 (https://netutgafan.snerpa.is/snorri/gylf.htm).
   - English: Arthur Gilchrist Brodeur, The Prose Edda (American-Scandinavian Foundation, 1916), via the
     sacred-texts.com transcription.

   No new rights are claimed over these texts or over the automatic alignment and modernisation derived
   from them (aligned/, auto/).

2. Contributions (CC BY 4.0)

   Everything added by contributors — overlay records in overlays/, image records and captions in images/,
   documentation — is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0).

   You are free to share and adapt this material for any purpose, including commercially, provided you give
   appropriate credit (name the project and the contributors listed in the records), link to the licence
   and indicate if changes were made.

   Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
   Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   By contributing you agree that your contribution is licensed CC BY 4.0. The project is considering a
   change to CC0 1.0 for contributions; contributors will be asked before any such change applies to their
   work.

